Proposed (16.7s): Use whenever the user has a Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, or YouTube analytics export (Insights, Studio, Creator export, or a platform CSV/XLSX) and wants the numbers looked at — analyze, compare, summarize, crunch, wrap up, or report on engagement, reach, CTR, views, RPM, follower growth, or revenue, for one period or across periods. Trigger whether or not they say "report": "how did engagement compare month over month," "which videos drove growth," "did reach actually go down," "wrap up the monthly numbers" all count, not just explicit "build/generate a report" requests. Covers monthly and yearly requests, including yearly ones built from partial or staggered monthly files. Delivers a client-ready PDF: computes engagement rate, CTR, follower growth, and revenue, normalizes for day-count differences, benchmarks against industry defaults, and renders through a locked template. One platform per run. Not for: ad-account issues, content calendars, captions, auto-posting scripts, or non-social data like financial/sales/email spreadsheets.

